1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,200
An animated eye is easy.
Making it look at you is not.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,600
Most of these wander on a timer.
This one is watching me.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:10,000
A tiny AI camera under the eye
finds my face on its own.

4
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:13,200
No Pi. No PC. No wifi.

5
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:16,800
The camera sends the face position
over two wires.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,400
A Teensy points the eye
at whatever the camera found.

7
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,000
The blinking and the pupil
are its own idea.

8
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:27,400
About $64 of parts.
A second eye is under $12.

9
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:31,000
None of this was the point.

10
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:34,600
The sensor my robot face used
got discontinued.

11
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:38,500
That face is called IRIS.
It is running this right now.
